        <name>universal_vector</name>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A <computeroutput>universal_vector</computeroutput> is a container that supports random access to elements, constant time removal of elements at the end, and linear time insertion and removal of elements at the beginning or in the middle. The number of elements in a <computeroutput>universal_vector</computeroutput> may vary dynamically; memory management is automatic. The memory associated with a <computeroutput>universal_vector</computeroutput> resides in memory accessible to hosts and devices.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/vector">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/vector</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classthrust_1_1host__vector" kindref="compound">host_vector</ref> For the documentation of the complete interface which is shared by <computeroutput>universal_vector</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
